# Drafted by Gemini (R14 stables), edited.

~ landers
Narrator: The stables smell of damp straw, lathered flanks, and cheap red wine. Three knights in their padded doublets pass a dented tin jug between the stalls.
landers_knight [smile]: Come in out of the frost, friends! A clean run down the valley and three strays brought to the Rose's fold. Pour yourselves a cup!
* Raise a cup to the Hunt's catch. -> landers_toast
* Did you bring in a tall Brightsinger pilgrim? -> landers_pilgrim
* Draw steel on them. -> stable_fight
* Leave them to their drink. -> END

~ landers_toast
Narrator: You tip the sour vintage back, and Landers slaps the stall door hard enough to make the iron rings rattle.
landers_knight [smile]: That is the spirit! A warm fire in the courtyard and a full cup in the straw, nothing finer on the mountain.
set crimson_devotions += 1
-> landers

~ landers_pilgrim
landers_knight [neutral]: Grey eyes, short beard? Aye, we roped him near the timber line. Stubborn fellow, sang his little bird-hymns all the way up the switchbacks.
-> landers

~ marla
marla_knight [smile]: Do you fancy horses, stranger? You should have seen Ser Maric try to mount the big black mare at dusk. Threw himself into a snowdrift and called it a flanking maneuver!
-> END

~ fremont
Narrator: Fremont leans against a tack post, paring his thumbnail with a skinning knife. His eyes flick once toward the iron key-ring high on the beam, then back to you.
fremont_knight [neutral]: Drink if you are drinking, pilgrim. A wise guest keeps his eyes on his cup and off the wall hooks.
-> END

~ stable_fight
landers_knight [angry]: Well now, look who brought bare iron to a friendly toast. Up, lads!
combat mon_stable_knights

~ hand
Narrator: A lanky boy in a mire-stained smock sweeps the same dry patch of cobbles over and over, his knuckles white on the broom handle.
stable_hand_cm [afraid]: Keep your voice down, please. The knights have sharp ears when the wine is in them, and I already said too much to that jailed singer.
* What did you whisper to the pilgrim? -> hand_secret
* How does one reach the sanctum below? -> hand_sanctum
* Step away from him. -> END

~ hand_secret
stable_hand_cm [afraid]: I swept the Abbot's study while he was at bells and saw his open ledger. The Crimson Rose is no goddess at all, she is a pit devil drinking our pain.
-> hand

~ hand_sanctum
stable_hand_cm [weary]: The stair goes down right under the high altar, if you have the stomach for it. They keep the silver chalice that works the lock behind the red dossal curtain.
set src_axel
set way_down_known
quest crimson_monastery the_way_down
-> hand

~ armory
Narrator: Racks of boar-spears and crimson shields line the dry stone wall. In a place of honour at the far end hangs a battered heater shield, its old gold leaf showing through the red paint.
give shield_of_marius_renathyr
set armory_shield
-> END

~ treats
Narrator: A slatted crate by the feed bins holds joints of raw, dripping knuckle-meat meant for the bat-hounds. Taking clergy stores will not be forgiven if anyone sees your hand in the straw.
give bloody_treats
set treats_taken
-> END
